WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.530
- [Narrator] These are tiltrotors

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:02.430
and they help explain,

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:05.046
why the US military's
Osprey is so valuable.

00:00:05.046 --> 00:00:06.990
When the rotors are tilted up,

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:08.880
the aircraft can take off, land,

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:10.410
and hover like a helicopter.

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:11.640
When they're tilted down,

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:12.750
it can fly as fast

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:14.153
and as high as an airplane.

00:00:14.153 --> 00:00:17.370
But the Osprey once dubbed,
"The Impossible Bird"

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:18.272
by the US military

00:00:18.272 --> 00:00:20.552
is now being called a "Flying Coffin"

00:00:20.552 --> 00:00:22.770
and a "Widowmaker" by critics.

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:24.990
And it's being grounded just as the US

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:26.130
and its Pacific partners,

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:27.210
were using the Osprey

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:29.790
to train for a potential
conflict with China.

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:32.040
So here's what we know.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:33.870
As tensions rise over Taiwan

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:35.130
and the South China Sea,

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:37.170
a key part of US strategy in the region,

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:38.580
involves rotating troops

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:41.250
around hundreds of small
islands near China.

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:43.085
The thinking is that those stand-in forces

00:00:43.085 --> 00:00:45.211
can strike fast, confuse the enemy,

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:47.807
and gather intelligence
about the battlefield.

00:00:47.807 --> 00:00:50.850
And that makes the Osprey
incredibly important

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.552
since it can cover vast distances,

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:53.880
land on ships,

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:55.920
and drop down on remote islands.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:58.099
We saw the Osprey's
usefulness during an exercise

00:00:58.099 --> 00:00:59.910
in the Philippines in April,

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:02.780
after taking an Army Black
Hawk helicopter out to a ship,

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:06.210
a 250 mile ride, that took three hours.

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:07.860
We then boarded this Osprey,

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:10.200
which flew roughly twice as fast.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.700
The Osprey was able to take off

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:13.031
from the deck in helicopter mode,

00:01:13.031 --> 00:01:16.680
zoom across the Luzon
Strait in airplane mode,

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:20.400
and then land on remote islands
just 100 miles from Taiwan.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:23.130
There troops hauled all
kinds of gear and weapons

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:25.110
onto the island to simulate a defense

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:27.630
of both the Philippines and Taiwan.

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:29.520
- The standing force is that force

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:31.380
that's inside the first island chain.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:32.880
They will move out into this terrain

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:34.860
and be able to provide security

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:36.053
to the people on this island,

00:01:36.053 --> 00:01:39.193
as well as secure it for
follow-on operations.

00:01:39.193 --> 00:01:40.980
- [Narrator] The Osprey has been used

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:41.865
in similar exercises

00:01:41.865 --> 00:01:43.260
across the Pacific,

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:46.020
from Australia, to Korea, to Japan.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:47.310
But in the past few years,

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:48.657
it has suffered deadly crashes.

00:01:48.657 --> 00:01:51.210
Some have been attributed to human error,

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:54.000
while others have been
caused by mechanical issues.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.882
Sadly, these fatal crashes
aren't a new phenomenon.

00:01:56.882 --> 00:01:58.242
Since it began flying,

00:01:58.242 --> 00:02:00.106
Osprey accidents have claimed the lives

00:02:00.106 --> 00:02:03.097
of more than 60 service
members and passengers.

00:02:03.097 --> 00:02:05.940
After a fatal crash in Japan in November,

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:08.370
the US suspended its entire fleet

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:09.870
for the first time ever

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:11.010
and some experts told me

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:13.230
that depending on what
the investigation finds,

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:14.310
it could be a year

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:16.050
until the Ospreys are flying again.

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:17.820
- We won't let them back into the air

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.170
until we know that we can do it

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:21.610
with a measure of certainty.

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:24.510
- [Narrator] So what does
this mean for US readiness

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.399
in the Pacific and around the world?

00:02:26.399 --> 00:02:28.740
The grounding could harm the US' ability

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:30.960
to execute a number of missions quickly,

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:33.630
like raids, evacuations, and resupply.

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:35.129
All things the Osprey helped carry out,

00:02:35.129 --> 00:02:37.620
during US wars in the Middle East.

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:39.510
And former Deputy Secretary of Defense,

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:42.180
Robert Work, says the suspension
will deal a major blow

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:43.110
to the Marines

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:45.768
since many of their operations
revolve around the platform.

00:02:45.768 --> 00:02:47.377
For now, the Marines say

00:02:47.377 --> 00:02:50.040
they still have confidence in the Osprey.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:51.120
And while it's grounded,

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:53.310
a range of aircraft will
be used in its place

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:56.040
to transport equipment,
supplies, and personnel.

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:57.840
Marines will also continue to prepare

00:02:57.840 --> 00:02:59.340
for future Osprey missions

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:02.160
by using simulators and
conducting maintenance.

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:04.680
A new plane for the army called the V-280

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:07.560
has been hailed as the next
generation of tiltrotors,

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:09.540
but deployment could be years away.

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:12.296
As for China, the foreign
ministry criticized the US,

00:03:12.296 --> 00:03:13.939
following the Osprey crash in Japan,

00:03:13.939 --> 00:03:16.844
saying that the US is acting recklessly

00:03:16.844 --> 00:03:19.086
while claiming to maintain regional peace

00:03:19.086 --> 00:03:21.989
and stability in China's backyard.

00:03:21.989 --> 00:03:26.563
(aircraft buzzing)

